# Policy data for the dev loop gate checks.
#
# WHY: the model-check-required allow and deny lists, its line cap, and the
# agent-git in-scope paths and command patterns used to live as shell literals
# in two scripts. Keeping them as data here lets one evaluator apply one rule
# order, so the checks cannot drift apart and a policy change is reviewable in
# one place.
#
# Format: one key=value per line. A blank line separates records. A line that
# starts with # is a comment. The value is everything after the first =. Keys
# are id, effect, principal, action, resource, match, case, when (repeatable),
# when_ere, and label. An unknown key is an error.
#
# Evaluation: default deny. A matching forbid wins over any matching permit.
# The first matching forbid in file order decides, else the first matching
# permit, else default.deny. A rule matches on action, on resource (glob by
# default), and on every when condition. when_ere is a POSIX ERE matched
# against the text attribute.

id=mcr.deny.github
effect=forbid
principal=*
action=skip-model-check
resource=.github/*
case=lower

